<ProseLayout
  title="How we make money"
  description="Selected by Men is an Amazon Associate. How commission works, whether we take brand units, and why Amazon is the storefront."
  eyebrow="The money"
  heading="How we make money"
>
  <p>This is the dry page. About is the desk. Standards is the filter.</p>

  <h2>Commission</h2>
  <p>
    Selected by Men is a participant in the Amazon Associates Program. Product
    links go to Amazon. If you buy through one of those links, Amazon pays this
    site a commission. The rate is Amazon’s, by category. We do not set it. We
    do not reorder a list because one category pays more than another.
  </p>
  <p>Clicking a link does not change the price you pay.</p>

  <h2>Amazon is the storefront</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not independent of Amazon. Product links go there because that
    is where we can check price, stock, and a large sample of verified owner
    reviews in one place, and because a commission on those purchases is how the
    site is paid. We do not pretend that is neutrality. We do not pretend Amazon
    is the only shop that exists. It is the shop this ranking uses.
  </p>
  <p>
    Brands cannot buy a ranking. Amazon’s commission rate cannot buy one either.
  </p>

  <h2>Brand units</h2>
  <p>
    We do not accept payment for placement. Unsolicited PR boxes do not get a
    review.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we ask for a sample or a loan to check a claim, and we use it, the guide
    will say so. A sample does not buy a ranking. Live guides on this site are
    based on manufacturer specifications, current listings, owner reviews, and
    published editorial tests — not on a box that arrived from a brand.
  </p>

  <h2>If a pick disappears</h2>
  <p>
    We replace it or we change the ranking. We do not keep a dead button.
    Cadence and the rest of the editorial rule are on <a href="/standards/">Standards</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How often this is reviewed</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial lists: at least every 90 days, or when the product or the facts
    move. That is on <a href="/standards/">Standards</a>. This page changes if the business model
    changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices</h2>
  <p>
    Prices in guides are typical US Amazon listings as of the guide’s updated
    date. They move. Check the live page.
  </p>

  <p><em>Last updated August 28, 2026.</em></p>
</ProseLayout>
